cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Parallel Numerical Library
authors:
  - family-names: Badejo
    given-names: Olajide
abstract: >-
  A C++20 numerical library whose twelve iterative solvers run behind seven
  interchangeable execution backends, serial, OpenMP, POSIX threads,
  std::jthread, MPI, hybrid MPI with OpenMP and CUDA, so that identical work can
  be timed under each programming model on one machine. Every shared memory
  backend produces bit identical iterates at every worker count under a
  deterministic fixed chunk reduction, and the study prices what holding that
  invariant costs.
license: MIT
# Tracks the project() version in CMakeLists.txt. Phase E5 bumps both to 1.1.0.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-02'
repository-code: https://github.com/Olajide-Badejo/Parallel-Numerical-Library
keywords:
  - numerical methods
  - parallel computing
  - reproducibility
  - benchmarking
notes: >-
  Built by its owner driving an AI coding agent from written specifications. The
  specifications and the design decisions are the owner's, the agent produced
  code and prose under them, and every number in the repository comes from a run
  on the owner's machine.
